- THE FORM, for each row:
  - the PARENT shell exports BGCHECK_LEDGER=run-logs/<tag>-<UTC stamp>.ledger.jsonl and BGCHECK_TAG=$(bgcheck newtag);
  - it runs the row in a CHILD `bash -c '...'`. The child registers ITSELF (--winpid of its own $$, --msyspid $$), runs the row's
    runlog command, and ends in `exit $rc`, so it never execs;
  - after the child has ended, the parent runs mirror/conhosts.py 8b9e4bf106d5 with the parent's winpid and the child's winpid
    (the child's is read from the ledger's record). It records every conhost.exe under either, with its parent pid and creation
    time, plus each pid's own creation time if it is still running;
  - then the parent runs `bgcheck check` (944e9ad8ce64, unchanged).
