AMENDMENT 5c.2 (the orchestrator's two additions on accepting 5c.1, frozen before D1 runs; nothing in 5c.1 has run).
- 1. D1'S PRECEDENCE AND MIXTURES. d1_26.py classes each of sea-obj's cells once, by the first class that fits, and prints the COUNT per
  class.
  - D1's reading is the MOST SEVERE class present: different > geom-only > reordered > subset > identical.
  - A MIXTURE WITHOUT "different" (any combination of identical, subset, reordered and geom-only) maps to the (b) family explicitly,
    under the table's reordered and geom-only rows: the same pieces as drawn geometry, so the cause is order.
  - Any "different" present makes the reading (1) plus order. The count of "different" cells is stated beside the others.
- 2. D4, THE WATER DECOMPOSITION (D3's water twin): mirror/d4_26.mts 3accaf9fd35c, from dry-clone/proxy, under the egress block, after D3.
  - At the 11 points where the water multisets differed (KJFK KLGA KEWR MIDTOWN KMIA KSFO KSEA KDTW BUFFALO ROUSES ZAPATA), each side's
    water rings are split by source.
  - ATTRIBUTION IS THE BUILDER'S OWN: report.sea.ringIdx, the positions of the sea rings in the package's water section (build.ts:265,
    by object identity). Every other ring is TIGER-sourced. So D4 is not an improvised attribution.
  - NEW uses R5c-2's reports. OLD uses R5c-1's control reports. Those are the reports of the builds that made cp-out's exact bytes; the
    tool checks each control package's sha against cp-out's, else INSTRUMENT.
  - ringIdx's size against drawn - dropped is recorded beside each point.
  - THE TIGER RULE:
    - rung 4 drops the smallest-area rings from ALL water rings, sea included (budget.ts:123-124);
    - the report counts the sea ones (report.sea.dropped);
    - so TIGER drops per side = PROVENANCE's dropped.water - report.sea.dropped.
    - The TIGER difference must be one-sided, on the side those counts say, and of size exactly |TIGER drops(NEW) - TIGER drops(OLD)|:
      a budget consequence.
  - Anything else in TIGER water is a REAL water difference -> STOP, to Daniel. The 14 read sha-equal TIGER files, so it would be a
    builder defect.
  - THE SEA PART (its only-new / only-old) is recorded: what D1 explains.
